	(lib_symbols)
	(text_box "DESIGN NOTES - TEST DEBUG\n\nLOGIC ANALYSER HEADER for Kingst LA5016: 2x20 2.54 mm KEYED box header, 40-way cable.\nKey-side row (odd pins, verify pin 1 vs cable triangle): 1-15 CH0-CH7, 17 GND, 19-33 CH8-CH15, 35 GND, 37 PWM1, 39 PWM2.\nOther row (even pins): 18 GND, 36 GND, rest NC - reserved for LA5032 CH16-31 (future upgrade).\nEach signal via 0R/100R series resistor at the header (short stub, can be cut).\nCH0 I2C SCL | CH1 I2C SDA | CH2 GPS PPS | CH3 GPS TX->P4 | CH4 m1421 SUTX | CH5 m1421 SURX (after mux) | CH6 m1421 SYNC | CH7 m1421 SD26 (1090 activity)\nCH8 P4 UART0 TX | CH9 C5 UART0 TX | CH10 User UART TX | CH11 m1421 SD27 (UAT activity) | CH12 PM ALERT | CH13 CHG INT/PD ALERT | CH14 P4 DBG_A | CH15 P4 DBG_B\nPWM1/PWM2 are LA OUTPUTS: to test pads; PWM1 also via DNP 0R to GPS PPS net (simulate PPS without GPS fix).\nTEST POINTS: every power rail (VBUS_USER, VBAT, VSYS, 5V, 5V_SDR, 5V_LCD, all 3V3 branches, P4 core rails, 3V3_DEV), GND test points near each, Kelvin pads on all PAC1954 shunts."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
